From: CoreRouter <noreply@corerouter>
Subject: [PATCH] net: no fallback tunnel devices by default

With the tunnel drivers built in (=y), each one creates its catch-all
device in the initial namespace while the initcalls run: gre0, gretap0,
erspan0, ip6gre0, ip6tnl0, sit0, tunl0. The sysctl that turns them off
(net.core.fb_tunnels_only_for_init_net=2) is applied from the command
line only after the initcalls, too late. CoreRouter (G1.6m) creates
every tunnel it uses through netlink and never relies on a catch-all
device; they only showed up as "not managed" interfaces. Start the
sysctl at 2 (no fallback devices in any namespace); it can still be
set back to 0 or 1 at run time for namespaces created afterwards.

---
--- a/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c
+++ b/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 
 static int net_msg_warn;	/* Unused, but still a sysctl */
 
-int sysctl_fb_tunnels_only_for_init_net __read_mostly = 0;
+int sysctl_fb_tunnels_only_for_init_net __read_mostly = 2;
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(sysctl_fb_tunnels_only_for_init_net);
 
 /* 0 - Keep current behavior:
